.TH LIBMPQ__UPDATE_REPLACE_RANGES_IDENTITY 3 2026-11-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__update_replace_ranges_identity \- replace fixed-size ranges in one exact staged MPQ identity
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__update_replace_ranges_identity("
.BI "        mpq_update_s *" "update,"
.BI "        const char *" "filename,"
.BI "        uint16_t " "locale,"
.BI "        uint16_t " "platform,"
.BI "        const mpq_update_replace_range_s *" "ranges,"
.BI "        size_t " "range_count"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Selects the exact \fIfilename\fP, \fIlocale\fP and \fIplatform\fP tuple.
The neutral tuple (0, 0) is exact. Other identities sharing safely detachable
classic storage retain their original content. Unsupported or ambiguous
extended identity provenance returns LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT.
.PP
Range validation, lossless storage, ownership, resource use and transaction
rules are the same as for libmpq__update_replace_ranges(3).
This includes the v2 extent check for nonempty edits and the no-op behavior
for a validated empty batch.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
/* update is a live transaction. The US English platform\N'45'0 member
 * has at least nine logical bytes. These edits leave the size unchanged. */
int32_t
stage_english_range_edits(mpq_update_s *update)
{
    const uint8_t marker[] = { 0x4d, 0x50, 0x51 };
    const uint8_t revision[] = { 0x02 };
    const mpq_update_replace_range_s ranges[] = {
        { .offset = 0, .data = marker, .size = sizeof(marker) },
        { .offset = 8, .data = revision, .size = sizeof(revision) }
    };
    const size_t count = sizeof(ranges) / sizeof(ranges[0]);

    return libmpq__update_replace_ranges_identity(
        update, "data/sample.bin", 0x0409, 0, ranges, count
    );
}
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fB0\fP on success or a negative libmpq error.
.SH ERRORS
LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST indicates a missing argument or live identity.
LIBMPQ_ERROR_SEEK indicates a negative range offset.
LIBMPQ_ERROR_SIZE indicates a range outside the member, unrepresentable
capacity, or an unsupported size or extent.
LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT indicates an unsupported representation or ambiguous
identity. LIBMPQ_ERROR_READ also covers checksum or validation mismatches.
Allocation, decryption, codec and I/O errors are reported by the transaction.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__update_commit (3),
.BR libmpq__update_replace_ranges (3)
